            "review_title": "Review at Gang Yu Hot Pot",
            "review_text": "hoanghac13\nSan Jose, California641 contributions\n0\nRoom for improvement and better working environment for female worker\nMay 2025 • Family\nGang Yu hotpot\nDuring my 7-day stay in Da Nang, I craved spicy hot pot and found a highly rated spot on Google. I walked 20-25 minutes from my hotel, arriving just past 7 PM. We opted for the all-you-can-eat combo for two, choosing spicy Sichuan and a sour Tom Yum-like soup. The restaurant was quiet—only 2-3 tables downstairs, and an upstairs area with possible large party. The Sichuan soup outshined the Tom Yum, which was bland and disappointing, especially since reviews hyped it as the second-best soup. Service was slow even with 3-4 servers. In the kitchen, male meat cutters were flirting with a female waitress, who tried to deflect but struggled until I glared at one, signaling, “Where’s my meat?” Initially, the beef was thinly sliced and great, but after a few rounds, the slices thickened, becoming tough and ruining our vibe. I gave three stars for the spicy soup and overall meat quality. I hope they improve service and consistency for picky eaters like me.\nRead more\nWritten May 6, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
